---
Static analysis via local cppcheck script (no CI per user preference).

User wants ZERO GitHub Actions on this repo. The CI half of the
original task is intentionally NOT done; the local script half is.

## What landed
- scripts/lint.sh — runs cppcheck on src/ and tests/, excludes deps/.
  Same flags an external CI would use, so dropping into a CI is a
  copy-paste job if the preference ever changes.
- cppcheck-suppressions.txt — suppression list for known false
  positives (starts empty, grows as findings surface).
- Inline suppressions via `// cppcheck-suppress xxx` work too via
  --inline-suppr.

## What did NOT land (and won't)
- GitHub Actions workflow (.github/workflows/*.yml) — explicitly
  rejected. Don't reintroduce.

## How to use
- `./scripts/lint.sh` — local run. Returns non-zero on `error`-level
  findings, so it can be wired into a pre-commit hook by hand if the
  user wants.
- Install on Fedora: `dnf install cppcheck`
- Install on Debian/Ubuntu: `apt-get install cppcheck`

## Acceptance Criteria (revised)
- [x] Local run script: ./scripts/lint.sh
- [x] Suppressions file for known false positives (vendored deps)
- [x] Critical/error findings cause non-zero exit (gateable by any
      external automation the user chooses to add later)
- [x] Warnings reported but don't fail
- [ ] ~~Static analysis runs in GitHub Actions CI~~  — REJECTED

## Test Plan
- [ ] After installing cppcheck, run ./scripts/lint.sh — should
      complete without errors on the current tree (or surface real
      findings to address)
- [x] Verify vendored code (deps/) is excluded — handled via -i deps
      in lint.sh
